{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/567293-2-5e-solar-melee-charms-dual-wielding-cascade","id":567293,"title":"[2.5e Solar Melee Charms] - Dual Wielding Cascade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T20:51:06-07:00","id":567293,"title":"[2.5e Solar Melee Charms] - Dual Wielding Cascade","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I last posted my first go at a dual-weapon Solar Melee Charm a few weeks back and got a lot of great responses. I've finalized that Charm, and came up with a couple others to build on those concepts. Mechanically speaking, I feel the effects aren't overpowered themselves, but the costs need to be balanced properly. That said, once again I'm looking for honest comments and criticism. Thanks for your time!<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Sun and Moon Stance</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2013 (3m); <b>Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Permanent;<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Martial-ready<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver beckons, and the blade responds \u2013 she feels no hindrance by habitual practices of handedness, for by her will such limits become obsolete. The Solar no longer suffers penalties specifically for wielding weapons in her off hand, regardless of which task her primary hand is engaged in. She feels equally at ease with the unwieldy pairing of hammer and axe as she does parrying attacks with a sword in her off hand while her forehand picks the locks of a chained ally.<br /> Furthermore, while wielding two weapons the Solar need not choose which weapon she attempts to deflect attacks with \u2013 \u201cboth\u201d is an equally-viable option. When subjected to an attack, the Lawgiver may spend 3m in step 2 to apply the \u201cDefense\u201d statistic from both weapons he is wielding to his DV for this attack. As this additional bonus provided comes from equipment, albeit applied originally via Essence manipulation, it does not count as a dice bonus from Charms. With a second purchase of this Charm at Essence 3, further activations of this Charm by the Lawgiver stack reduce its cost by 1m per prior activation, to a minimum of 0m, until his next action. A second activation of Sun and Moon Stance within the same action costs 2m, a third costs 1m, and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Twin Heavens Crossing</span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental;<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Combo-OK, Martial-ready, Obvious<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>One Weapon, Two Blows; Sun and Moon Stance<br /> <br /> Twin blades that defend as one may also kill as one. A Lawgiver wielding two weapons may just as easily strike with both blades as he might with one. This Charm enables the Solar to strike a target simultaneously with a weapon (melee, ranged, or even natural) in each hand as a single action. This action may be performed alone, or as part of a flurry, and has a Speed equivalent to that of the weapon with the highest value among the two. This action counts as a single attack for the purposes of flurries, Excellencies, extra-action Charms, and the evaluation of attack event steps 3-6. The attacker makes a single roll, combining the accuracy bonuses of both weapons, and applies it once against the defender\u2019s DV. If it hits, steps 7-10 proceed individually for each weapon, each using the net successes from the single attack and applying damage from both simultaneously in step 10. Onslaught penalties are applied cumulatively at the end of both attacks (a combined total of -2).<br /> This Charm may be applied to weapons utilizing different Abilities \u2013 a Firewand and Daiklave is as valid a pairing as is a Goremaul and a Smashfist or Grimcleaver and Sky-Cutter. However, when this Charm is used in a Combo containing other Charms for the purposes of enhancing attacks with weapons that use different abilities, the resulting Combo must obey all rules as normal. Other Charms within the Combo must be capable of enhancing both Abilities \u2013 a combo of this Charm and Essence Arrow Attack used in application with a Goremaul and Firewand would be considered invalid, because the latter Charm cannot Supplement Melee actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Two Become One</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>\u2013; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 4; <b>Type:</b> Permanent;<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Duration:</b> \u2013<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Twin Heavens Crossing<br /> <br /> Against the Lawgiver\u2019s twin blades, no foe will stand and no armor will protect. This Charm enhances its prerequisite. When an attack with two weapons is supplemented with Twin Heavens Crossing, each attack is no longer separately for the purposes of steps 7-10 \u2013 instead, the raw damage of both weapons is combined and applied as one against the defender\u2019s soak. This does not allow the Solar to supersede dice adder caps for damage-modifying Charms such as Fire and Stones Strike - the declaration of such Charms in Step 1 with Twin Heavens Crossing (as enhanced by Two Become One) must respect the net dice caps imposed by the effects of this Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","user":"Whisper","date":". 06-25-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:29:03-07:00","id":567357,"title":"","content":"Looks good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:42:28-07:00","id":568033,"title":"","content":"Thanks! What do you think of the cost? 5m was a guess by me, but I'm wondering if that's right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:16:06-07:00","id":569301,"title":"","content":"Man those crickets are painful. 58 views and only one response? Whatever the response, I value feedback. Don't feel the need to hold back folks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T13:22:10-07:00","id":573075,"title":"","content":"Looks good to me, but I'm more of a 1st ed. guy. I like the 3rd charm where the damage is dded together for Soak. Devastating. When combined with an excellency and a damage multiplier, it would be pretty crazy.<br /> <br /> Edit, i just realized you limited damage adding charms. Smart for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> Edit2: looks like its still compatible with Hungry Tiger, so...ouch. and compatible with extra action charms as well.....no wonder they are Essence 5 Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":779,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","user":"NuSoardGraphite","date":". 06-29-2015, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:32:45-07:00","id":574036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/567293-2-5e-solar-melee-charms-dual-wielding-cascade?p=573075#post573075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks good to me, but I'm more of a 1st ed. guy. I like the 3rd charm where the damage is dded together for Soak. Devastating. When combined with an excellency and a damage multiplier, it would be pretty crazy.<br /> <br /> Edit, i just realized you limited damage adding charms. Smart for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> Edit2: looks like its still compatible with Hungry Tiger, so...ouch. and compatible with extra action charms as well.....no wonder they are Essence 5 Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Yeah, I wanted to make sure that Two Become One didn't break dice adder caps. It felt kind of weird, but I think the end result is better than allowing a dual-wielding solar to inadvertently double his dice caps for damage modifiers with this Charm by paying for each attack before combining them. The net result of the Charm is that you basically get a slight buff to your base raw damage, at the expense of making it only one attack that needs to be perfectly soaked instead of two. At the high end of play (vs Solaroids/Celestials) it's strong, but far from game-breaking, and it absolutely destroys anything that lacks perfects and can't parry/dodge the attack.<br /> <br /> It's not Essence 5 - Twin Heavens Crossing is Essence 3, and Two Become One is Essence 4. However, at 5m per activation (tentative cost), it's not cheap to use in flurries or with Extra Action Charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6293-whisper","name":"Whisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:21:11-07:00","id":575066,"title":"","content":"This has been a big thing I wanted to do with second edition... but I think jumping into charms right off the bat to hastily is a mistake. Think of mortal use... what merit would they get? Ambidextrous would be a start... after that improve on a grand scale. One of the solutions that I lost allowed you to pick an aspect to combine, at the purchase you'd pick accuracy, damage or defense; while your rate increased by half your essence.<br /> <br /> I need to go over your charms again later... lol i have two kids on the rtrain and i'm all most in penn station","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i712.photobucket.com/albums/ww125/PaulJustus/FireAspectink_zpsf63a29e6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />My <a href=\"http://layton224.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DA</a> page","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","name":"layton224","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2926_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T20:20:48-07:00","id":583104,"title":"","content":"These are a few ideas <br /> <br /> Dual weapon fighting <br /> <br /> Mundane rules: a player without any merit or enhancements, uses the best attributes of the two weapons. This is until they reach the lower rate of the two and if the other weapon has higher rate, then you are restrained to that weapons attributes. And one weapon is subject to off hand penalty. <br /> <br /> Ambidextrous: negates off hand penalty. I know it's canan but just putting it out there. <br /> <br /> Combined (Attribute) Kata: The fighter has learned how to synchronize one of the weapons attributes, divide the lower attributes score in half rounded down and apply that to the higher one.<br /> <br /> Flailing Tiger Stance: half the penalty on flurries and cuts the DV penalty in half rounded up. <br /> <br /> Vicious Heads of the Hydra: The character's hands work independently, granting them an action for each hand. The parry DV from each of hands are combined and the dodge DV enjoys a -1 based penalty. If one weapon is in a guard action double it's parry DV and apply the penalty from it's mate normally, the dodge DV enjoys a +1 based. If both are in a guard action double the combined parry DV and the dodge DV enjoys +3 base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i712.photobucket.com/albums/ww125/PaulJustus/FireAspectink_zpsf63a29e6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />My <a href=\"http://layton224.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DA</a> page","edited":{"userid":2926,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","user":"layton224","date":".  Fix 07-07-2015, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","name":"layton224","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2926_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}